title: '[pallet_balances] Remove `FreezeIdentifier` and `MaxFreezes` in favour of `RuntimeFreezeReason`'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Closes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/2997, doing for freezes what
    https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/pull/2657 did for holds.

    `Freezes` was keyed by `FreezeIdentifier` and bounded by a hand written `MaxFreezes`, while
    `RuntimeFreezeReason`, the enum pallets actually freeze with, was used by nothing but an
    `integrity_test`. Both are now removed and `RuntimeFreezeReason` is the freeze id, with the
    vector bounded by `VariantCountOf<T::RuntimeFreezeReason>`, so the bound can no longer
    disagree with the enum.

    - `Config::RuntimeFreezeReason` gains the `Parameter + Member + MaxEncodedLen + Copy` bounds it
      needs as a stored id, and `fungible::InspectFreeze::Id` is now `T::RuntimeFreezeReason`.
    - The `MaxFreezes >= VARIANT_COUNT` `integrity_test` is dropped, and a new `freezes_decode`
      `try_state` check reports entries that do not decode under the new id type.
    - The `Balances::MaxFreezes` constant disappears from runtime metadata.

    ## Migration

    Drop `type FreezeIdentifier` and `type MaxFreezes` from every `pallet_balances::Config` impl.
    The `RuntimeFreezeReason` generated by `construct_runtime!` already satisfies the new bounds.

    No storage migration is required where `FreezeIdentifier` was already `RuntimeFreezeReason`,
    which is every runtime here: the encoding is unchanged and an account could never hold more
    freezes than there are freeze reasons. Runtimes that used a different `FreezeIdentifier` must
    translate their `Freezes` entries first, and can verify the result with `try_state`.
